# Wave W17-Y (Route 213): salt turf — salt-grass flats turf, pale salt flecks: a dry olive-khaki flat carrying silvery salt flecks where the flats crust white between the grass, the first dry country east of Fenland (design: pale salt flats spreading off the road, the lake shining through the trees at the end of it). Route 213’s own ground — split from Route 222’s beach turf ahead by the crust (salt pan vs open beach) and from Route 201’s fresh shore green by dryness entire: this grass grows on salt, that one on lake light.
